{"id":284,"name":"masquerain","speciesId":284,"dex":284,"form":"normal","generation":3,"types":["bug","flying"],"stats":{"hp":70,"attack":60,"defense":62,"special-attack":100,"special-defense":82,"speed":80},"abilities":[{"name":"intimidate","hidden":false},{"name":"unnerve","hidden":true}],"height":8,"weight":36,"baseExp":159,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/284.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/284.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/284.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/284.ogg","genus":"Eyeball Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"ruby","text":"MASQUERAIN intimidates enemies with the eyelike patterns on its antennas. This POKéMON flaps its four wings to freely fly in any direction - even sideways and backwards - as if it were a helicopter."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"MASQUERAIN’s antennas have eyelike patterns that usually give it an angry look. If the “eyes” are droopy and appear sad, it is said to be a sign that a heavy rainfall is on its way."},{"version":"emerald","text":"It intimidates foes with the large eyelike patterns on its antennae. Because it can’t fly if its wings get wet, it shelters itself from rain under large trees and eaves."},{"version":"firered","text":"The antennae have distinctive patterns that look like eyes. When it rains, they grow heavy, making flight impossible."},{"version":"diamond","text":"Its antennae have eye patterns on them. Its four wings enable it to hover and fly in any direction."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"It flaps its four wings to hover and fly freely in any direction-- to and fro and sideways."},{"version":"y","text":"It flaps its four wings to hover and fly freely in any direction--to and fro and sideways."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Masquerain in